Scholarly study — investigate and improve a measurement method (@met-independent-research: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metrology, #source "../sources/GUM-and-Amendment.lingua#r_3KA76CK3QAA3M470TC3XHP19MQ", #source "../sources/GUM-Models.lingua#r_3AAJPGTHAAF72R05SJ1VJ7HN46", #source "../sources/GUM-Monte-Carlo.lingua#r_79V20QP3T2KZ6GD07SK5TGZ1J4", #source "../sources/GUM-Multivariate.lingua#r_1S5554FGCGA5E8GKAM6C9KMJKK", #source "../sources/GUM-Conformity.lingua#r_0VFKYJZJC8BXM2T2TSY58DD6SY", #source "../sources/GUM-Examples-2026.lingua#r_4FVN1GYTH9X8M1JFWFNT696GR0", #source "../sources/Uncertainty-NIST-1900.lingua#r_75WCVW8CJG4TAFD3330T87588E", #metrology "Completion.lingua#r_53S7BF9JY2ZA1VT8820RXYR72Z") { r_3S2V3ZCFMX40WZ7QMMEZ1E66V3
**Read:** [GUM — JCGM 100:2008 and the 2026 nonlinearity amendment](../sources/GUM-and-Amendment.lingua#r_3KA76CK3QAA3M470TC3XHP19MQ), the full guide, amendment, and explanatory annexes; [Developing and using measurement models — JCGM GUM-6](../sources/GUM-Models.lingua#r_3AAJPGTHAAF72R05SJ1VJ7HN46), the whole document; [Propagation of distributions using Monte Carlo — JCGM 101](../sources/GUM-Monte-Carlo.lingua#r_79V20QP3T2KZ6GD07SK5TGZ1J4), the whole document; [Several output quantities — JCGM 102](../sources/GUM-Multivariate.lingua#r_1S5554FGCGA5E8GKAM6C9KMJKK), the whole document; [Measurement uncertainty in conformity assessment — JCGM 106](../sources/GUM-Conformity.lingua#r_0VFKYJZJC8BXM2T2TSY58DD6SY), the whole document; [Worked measurement examples — JCGM GUM-5:2026](../sources/GUM-Examples-2026.lingua#r_4FVN1GYTH9X8M1JFWFNT696GR0), the whole volume; [Simple Guide for Evaluating and Expressing Uncertainty — Possolo](../sources/Uncertainty-NIST-1900.lingua#r_75WCVW8CJG4TAFD3330T87588E), the complete report and worked examples.

Choose a focused measurement question that goes beyond reproducing a textbook example while remaining within the trail’s direction. Examples include a significant nonlinear correction, dependence introduced by a shared reference, a time-dependent response, a difficult sampling target, or a disagreement between two technically credible methods. A narrow question can require substantial physical and mathematical work.

Read the complete GUM suite volumes assigned here and TN 1900, then develop a literature review around the particular question. Find at least three independent technical treatments, including peer-reviewed research or national-laboratory/university reports and at least one source treating the physical measurement principle. Prefer open authorized editions. Retain actual authors, titles, dates, identifiers, method details, and exact passages; a bibliography collected without reading is not the review.

Reconstruct at least two substantive results independently, following the cited mathematical and physical preparation as needed. Compare measurand definitions, references, experimental conditions, data treatment, and uncertainty interpretation. Identify an actual disagreement, unresolved assumption, or limitation rather than inventing novelty from different notation.

Develop and test a bounded improvement or investigation. This can be a better design, a corrected inference, a sensitivity analysis showing when an approximation fails, an independently validated computation, or a physical comparison where facilities permit. Preserve observations or simulation definitions, code/settings when used, exact and numerical checks, and negative findings. Distinguish a demonstrated improvement from a proposal awaiting experimental evidence.

**Scholarly result:** write a substantial technical report with a precise question, source criticism, physical and statistical models, derivations, reproducible analysis, uncertainty and dependence, validation, limitations, and a reasoned conclusion. Make the scope narrow enough to defend and deep enough that an informed reader can challenge the work at the level of its actual methods.

Seek serious criticism, answer it through additional evidence or a revised claim, and retain that revision. Advanced completion requires understanding the tools well enough to explain their failure modes and choose among defensible alternatives, not only reproducing the official guide’s preferred example.

**Continue:** [What completing measurement and metrology means](Completion.lingua#r_53S7BF9JY2ZA1VT8820RXYR72Z).

